I'm going to check this out. I really feel the 'create a R dist and push' is the best way to go.
This should be checked on as many clusters as possible.

Of course,
- in a EC2 cluster, it's easy to install R on the nodes

- if the cluster has a DFS like LUSTRE that it would best still. For example,a cluster at Purdue has a Lustre filesystem hosting the home directories. Users can install RHIPE
in their home directory and a small shell script in rhoptions()$runner picks things up.

But for the rest of us, who are not admins and cannot get stuff installed on the nodes, make-R-ship is the best.

Saptarshi

